# EduFlow LMS — URL-Based API Architecture Plan

> **Core Rule**: The frontend contains **ZERO** educational content. No curriculum data, no chapter names, no topic lists, no questions, no syllabus. The frontend is a pure UI shell that calls API URLs and renders whatever comes back.

---

## 1. Complete API Endpoint Catalog

### 1.1 Configuration Endpoints (Populate Dropdowns)

These endpoints supply the options for the Settings panel selectors. The frontend renders empty `<select>` tags and populates them dynamically from API responses.

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/api/boards` | List all available education boards |
| `GET` | `/api/classes` | List all available class levels |
| `GET` | `/api/subjects` | List all available subjects |
| `GET` | `/api/file-types` | List all available content types (topics, syllabus, questions) |

### 1.2 Curriculum Content Endpoints

These are the core educational content endpoints. The frontend calls them based on the teacher's selected Board + Class + Subject combination.

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/api/curriculum/{board}/{class}/{subject}` | Get all topics for a specific board/class/subject |
| `GET` | `/api/curriculum/{board}/{class}/{subject}/chapters` | Get chapter list only |
| `GET` | `/api/curriculum/{board}/{class}/{subject}/syllabus` | Get syllabus outline |

### 1.3 Course & Module Endpoints (Future LMS Expansion)

| Method | Endpoint | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/api/courses` | List all available courses |
| `GET` | `/api/course/{courseId}` | Get course details (title, description, metadata) |
| `GET` | `/api/course/{courseId}/modules` | List all modules in a course |
| `GET` | `/api/module/{moduleId}` | Get single module content |
| `GET` | `/api/module/{moduleId}/topics` | Get topics within a module |
| `GET` | `/api/module/{moduleId}/questions` | Get questions/quizzes for a module |

### 1.4 Teacher Activity Endpoints (Existing Supabase — Already URL-Based)

These already work through the Supabase REST API. No changes needed.

| Method | Endpoint (Supabase auto-generated) | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `GET` | `/rest/v1/daily_activities?user_id=eq.{uid}` | Fetch teacher's daily entries |
| `POST` | `/rest/v1/daily_activities` | Save/upsert daily entries |
| `DELETE` | `/rest/v1/daily_activities?date=eq.{date}` | Delete a day's entries |

