### 3.2 Recommendation: Option C (Supabase PostgREST) for Phase 1

Since you are already using Supabase, the fastest path is:

1. **Store all educational content in PostgreSQL tables** (not CSV files)
2. **Use Supabase's built-in REST API** (PostgREST) — every table automatically gets REST endpoints
3. **Create database Views** for complex queries (e.g., joining boards + classes + subjects + topics)

This means:
- `GET /rest/v1/boards?select=id,name,display_order&order=display_order` → replaces `/api/boards`
- `GET /rest/v1/curriculum_topics?board=eq.CBSE&class=eq.10&subject=eq.Mathematics` → replaces `/api/curriculum/cbse/10/math`

**No custom backend server needed.** Supabase generates the REST API from your tables automatically.

### 3.3 Database Storage Design

```
┌─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┐
│                    Supabase PostgreSQL                    │
├─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┤
│                                                          │
│  boards           classes          subjects               │
│  ┌────────────┐  ┌────────────┐  ┌──────────────────┐   │
│  │ id         │  │ id         │  │ id               │   │
│  │ name       │  │ name       │  │ name             │   │
│  │ display_   │  │ display_   │  │ folder_key       │   │
│  │   order    │  │   order    │  │ display_order    │   │
│  │ is_active  │  │ is_active  │  │ is_active        │   │
│  └────────────┘  └────────────┘  └──────────────────┘   │
│         │               │               │                │
│         └───────────┬───┘───────────────┘                │
│                     │                                    │
│              curriculum_topics                           │
│              ┌──────────────────────┐                    │
│              │ id                   │                    │
│              │ board (TEXT)         │ ← denormalized     │
│              │ class (TEXT)         │   for simpler      │
│              │ subject (TEXT)       │   REST queries     │
│              │ chapter_number (INT) │                    │
│              │ chapter_name (TEXT)  │                    │
│              │ subtopic (TEXT)      │                    │
│              │ topic_tag (TEXT)     │                    │
│              │ display_order (INT) │                    │
│              └──────────────────────┘                    │
│                                                          │
│              daily_activities (existing, unchanged)       │
│              ┌──────────────────────┐                    │
│              │ user_id             │                    │
│              │ date                │                    │
│              │ period_number       │                    │
│              │ class_section       │                    │
│              │ classwork           │                    │
│              │ homework            │                    │
│              │ photo_url           │                    │
│              └──────────────────────┘                    │
└─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────┘
```

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Key Design Decision**: The `curriculum_topics` table uses denormalized TEXT columns (`board`, `class`, `subject`) instead of foreign key IDs. This makes the Supabase REST queries simpler: `?board=eq.CBSE&class=eq.10&subject=eq.Mathematics` instead of needing to join three tables. For a project of this scale, simplicity beats normalization.

