## 4. How the Frontend Should Consume These URLs

### 4.1 New Module: `js/api.js`

A single new file that encapsulates ALL API calls. No other file in the project makes direct `fetch()` calls to content endpoints.

```
api.js responsibilities:
├── fetchBoards()           → GET /rest/v1/boards
├── fetchClasses()          → GET /rest/v1/classes
├── fetchSubjects()         → GET /rest/v1/subjects
├── fetchCurriculum(board, class, subject)
│                           → GET /rest/v1/curriculum_topics?board=eq.{board}&class=eq.{class}&subject=eq.{subject}
├── fetchCourse(courseId)   → GET /rest/v1/courses?id=eq.{courseId}
├── fetchModules(courseId)  → GET /rest/v1/modules?course_id=eq.{courseId}
└── fetchQuestions(moduleId)→ GET /rest/v1/questions?module_id=eq.{moduleId}
```

### 4.2 Frontend Data Flow

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant User
    participant UI as ui.js
    participant API as api.js (NEW)
    participant SB as Supabase REST API
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Note over User,DB: Page Load — Settings Tab
    UI->>API: fetchBoards()
    API->>SB: GET /rest/v1/boards?order=display_order
    SB->>DB: SELECT * FROM boards ORDER BY display_order
    DB-->>SB: [CBSE, ICSE, State Board]
    SB-->>API: JSON response
    API-->>UI: Board list
    UI->>User: Populate Board dropdown

    UI->>API: fetchSubjects()
    API->>SB: GET /rest/v1/subjects?order=display_order
    SB-->>API: JSON response
    API-->>UI: Subject list
    UI->>User: Populate Subject dropdown

    Note over User,DB: User Saves Config → Daily Entry Tab
    User->>UI: Select CBSE / 10 / Mathematics / Save
    UI->>API: fetchCurriculum("CBSE", "10", "Mathematics")
    API->>SB: GET /rest/v1/curriculum_topics?board=eq.CBSE&class=eq.10&subject=eq.Mathematics&order=display_order
    SB->>DB: SELECT * FROM curriculum_topics WHERE ...
    DB-->>SB: 82 rows
    SB-->>API: JSON array of topic objects
    API-->>UI: Parsed topic tags
    UI->>User: Autocomplete hashtags now available (#Ch1_Real_Numbers, etc.)
```

### 4.3 What the Frontend Autocomplete Receives

Currently `autocomplete.js` reads from `window.CURRICULUM_TAGS["Mathematics"]` — an array of strings. This contract stays identical. The only change is **how that array gets populated**:

| Current (Hardcoded) | Proposed (URL-Based) |
|---|---|
| `curriculum.js` line 4: `window.CURRICULUM_TAGS = { "Mathematics": [...] }` | `api.js`: `fetch('/rest/v1/curriculum_topics?...').then(rows => rows.map(r => r.topic_tag))` |
| Data exists at page load | Data fetched asynchronously on page load |
| Fallback: local array | Fallback: empty array + error banner |

