## 6. Migration Strategy

### Phase 1: Database Setup (No Frontend Changes)

```
Step 1.1 → Create tables: boards, classes, subjects in Supabase SQL Editor
Step 1.2 → Seed boards: INSERT INTO boards (name, display_order) VALUES ('CBSE', 1), ('ICSE', 2), ('State Board', 3)
Step 1.3 → Seed classes: INSERT INTO classes (name, display_order) VALUES ('1', 1), ('2', 2), ... ('10', 10)
Step 1.4 → Seed subjects: INSERT INTO subjects (name, folder_key, display_order) VALUES ('Mathematics', 'math', 1), ...
Step 1.5 → Create curriculum_topics table with denormalized board/class/subject TEXT columns
Step 1.6 → Parse each local CSV file and INSERT rows into curriculum_topics
           (82 Math rows + ~100 Science rows + ~36 English rows + ~120 Social rows + ~30 Telugu rows)
Step 1.7 → Set up RLS policies: public read on all config tables, authenticated write
Step 1.8 → Verify: open Supabase REST API in browser:
           https://syjhiqlfjieihhpymwdz.supabase.co/rest/v1/boards?select=*
           → should return JSON array of boards
```

### Phase 2: Create `api.js` (New File, No Breaking Changes)

```
Step 2.1 → Create js/api.js with functions:
           - fetchBoards() → calls Supabase REST /rest/v1/boards
           - fetchClasses() → calls Supabase REST /rest/v1/classes
           - fetchSubjects() → calls Supabase REST /rest/v1/subjects
           - fetchCurriculumTopics(board, class, subject) → calls /rest/v1/curriculum_topics?...
           Each function uses the existing getSupabaseClient() to make authenticated requests.

Step 2.2 → Add <script src="js/api.js?v=4.0"></script> to index.html BEFORE curriculum.js
Step 2.3 → Test: call fetchBoards() from browser console, verify JSON response
```

### Phase 3: Rewire Frontend to Use API URLs (Breaking Changes)

```
Step 3.1 → curriculum.js: Replace window.CURRICULUM_TAGS hardcoded object with:
           window.CURRICULUM_TAGS = {};  // empty, populated by API
           
Step 3.2 → curriculum.js: Rewrite loadCurriculumCSV() to call:
           fetchCurriculumTopics(board, class, subject)
           instead of building a local file path and fetching CSV

Step 3.3 → index.html: Replace hardcoded <option> tags with empty <select> shells:
           <select id="settingsCurriculumBoard"></select>   ← populated by fetchBoards()
           <select id="settingsCurriculumClass"></select>    ← populated by fetchClasses()
           <select id="settingsCurriculumSubject"></select>  ← populated by fetchSubjects()

Step 3.4 → ui.js: Update loadSettingsUI() to call API and populate dropdowns dynamically

Step 3.5 → index.html: Same for Teacher Subject dropdown — populate from fetchSubjects()
```

