## Open Questions

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q1: Backend Choice** — Should we use Supabase's built-in PostgREST API (zero backend code, just tables) or build a custom Node.js/Express API server with clean `/api/curriculum/cbse/10/math` style URLs?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q2: CSV Parsing Location** — Currently the frontend parses raw CSV into topic tags. In the new architecture, should the CSV be parsed once during upload (a migration script converts CSV → database rows) and the API returns pre-structured JSON? Or should the API still serve raw CSV and the frontend parses it?

> [!IMPORTANT]
> **Q3: Content Seeding** — After migration, how should new curriculum content be added? Options: (A) Teacher uploads CSV via the app UI → backend parses and inserts, (B) Admin runs SQL INSERTs in Supabase Dashboard, (C) A separate admin script/tool that reads CSVs and populates the database.
